  "reasoning": "The patient presents with a combination of fever, headache, swollen lymph nodes, weakness, and fatigue. These are hallmark symptoms of a viral upper respiratory infection. Swollen lymph nodes alongside fever and fatigue strongly indicate an immune response to a common viral pathogen. While conditions like dengue or malaria cause fever and headache, they typically include additional distinguishing features such as severe body/joint pain, rashes, or cyclical chills and sweating, which are not reported here. Respiratory infections like pneumonia would prominently feature cough and breathing difficulties. Allergies generally do not cause fever. Given the symptom cluster without localized severe pain, rash, or chronic systemic signs, the clinical picture aligns best with a common cold.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]common cold[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}

